    "decision": "APPROVE WITH LIMITS for early development retention of this exact visual02 local crown appearance.",
    "net_whole_gain": "Small consistent positive tonal/source progress across Builder, Maker and Mechanic canon whole pairs under both supplied lights: front crown is cooler gray steel instead of broad pale warm cream/bronze, with less color separation from surrounding metal. This removes one distracting appearance mismatch at whole scale.",
    "visual01_cost": "Previously conspicuous disconnected polygon mosaic is absent in supplied exact visual02 views. Surface response is continuous in the canon/head view, and no new opposite/rear visual discontinuity is conspicuous.",
    "cost": "Fine streak/patch variation on the old cap is reduced; the resulting surface still reads smooth, blank and somewhat soft. This is a small simplification cost at head scale. Broad highlights remain bright in some head/side lights, so pale roof dominance is reduced in color more than eliminated in luminance.",
    "why_useful_despite_limits": "Within this narrow appearance scope, more coherent local steel tone and removal of visual01 mosaic outweigh that small surface-simplification cost. Optic, bronze edge, bill outline, stance and continuity stay readable in all supplied pairs; no meaningful new whole-character cost is apparent.",
